    "faq": [
        {
            "question": "Is AG Grid free?",
            "answer": "Yes. AG Grid Community is free for everyone under the MIT licence, including commercial and production use, and needs no licence key. AG Grid Enterprise needs a commercial licence in production. You can try Enterprise features locally without a licence key, with a watermark, or request a free 30-day trial licence. See [Community vs Enterprise](./community-vs-enterprise/) and [AG Grid pricing](/license-pricing/)."
        },
        {
            "question": "Is there a free alternative to AG Grid?",
            "answer": "If you are looking for a free alternative to AG Grid Enterprise, start with AG Grid Community. It is free under the MIT licence, and includes filtering, cell editing, row selection, CSV export and row and column virtualisation. You only need Enterprise for features such as row grouping, pivoting and Excel export. If your table is simple, a lighter free table library may be all you need. Our [comparisons](/compare/) show how AG Grid compares with other grids on features and licensing."
        },
        {
            "question": "What is the difference between AG Grid Community and Enterprise?",
            "answer": "AG Grid Community has the core features of a data grid: sorting, filtering, cell editing, row selection, CSV export and virtualisation. AG Grid Enterprise adds advanced features such as row grouping, aggregation, pivoting, tree data, set filters, Excel export and the AI Toolkit, with support through Zendesk. [Community vs Enterprise](./community-vs-enterprise/) lists every feature in each edition."
        },
        {
            "question": "Can I start with AG Grid Community and upgrade later?",
            "answer": "Yes. AG Grid Enterprise builds on AG Grid Community, so you keep the grid you have built. To upgrade, install the ag-grid-enterprise package, register the Enterprise modules you need and add your licence key. See [Install AG Grid Enterprise](./license-install/)."
        },
        {
            "question": "How is AG Grid Enterprise licensed?",
            "answer": "AG Grid Enterprise is licensed per developer and per deployment. Each licence is perpetual and includes one year of updates and support. See [AG Grid pricing](/license-pricing/) for prices."
        }
